{
  "about": "Shared cases for goals_sync_impl (Rust, goals_sync_contract_tests.rs) and its test port (goalsSyncPort.testing.ts). seed is synced first, concurrent is a foreign writer's field-level UPDATE/DELETE (what the MCP server does), then payload is synced. expect lists column values by table and id; absent lists ids that must be gone. A payload row with a matching base row (baseGoals/baseGoalRuns/baseStations) is a three-way update: only columns whose value differs from the base are written, and a row that no longer exists is not brought back. A row without a base is inserted or fully overwritten. A three-way update is also a compare-and-swap: when a column the payload changed was changed in the database too, to a different value, the whole row is left as the database has it and the sync reports it under conflicts (table, id, the columns that clash). updated_at is bookkeeping and never clashes. Cases without conflicts expect none.",
